{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/998847-what-stops-the-never-ending-arms-race","id":998847,"title":"What stops the never ending arms race?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-05T12:03:25-07:00","id":998847,"title":"What stops the never ending arms race?","content":"It seems to me, that thanks to the setting encouraging a somewhat militant mindset no matter WHAT faction you're aligned with, and the endless ways for mages to prepare for conflict, how do you guys prevent the game from turning into a mystical cold war for the soul of the world where the players are always working on that edge that will tip the odds in their favor just enough to turn the cold war hot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T12:14:25-07:00","id":998850,"title":"","content":"Personally?<br /> <br /> By focusing on plain, simple humans that suddenly can do magic, and are trying to cope with managing life, mage politics, duties, trying to hide their nature from sleepers, and studies of new mysteries, with a dash of saving X from doom. Without going into the whole 'Zomg we are all ruthless, magickal combat veterans in an endless war' spiel.<br /> <br /> People tend forget that there are mages who don't see a single mundane violent conflict in their lifetimes, and others that do, but are better at simply running for their lives.<br /> Combat needn't be a bad thing in the roleplay, but people way too often tend to act like every paradigm of every mage allows them to suddenly drop their enemy into magickal bulletinfernodoomspacehell, and that every mage is a cold blooded warrior that just goes ahead and does that because they can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T12:22:59-07:00","id":998853,"title":"","content":"Perhaps not ruthless magickal combat veterans. But being a mage means you're part of the ascension war. If only because the Technocracy will either kill or convert you simply for existing. The Technocracy is going to target your mundane life the moment they find out who you are. And it's worth noting they're very good at that.<br /> <br /> So unless you're going to become Frank Walker, Holed up in your paranoid fortress of a home, declaring yourself Switzerland. Which the game doesn't GENERALLY support given that the only ostensibly neutral tradition are the orphans. And they're neutral by virtue of isolation 90% of the time.<br /> <br /> And I'm not even saying that they have to be cold blooded or powerful. The setting simply drops every mage into a warzone and has two sides metaphorically shoving a wizard hat or a pair of mirrorshades at them. Demanding loyalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T12:26:23-07:00","id":998855,"title":"","content":"The Pogrom is over. Has been for over a decade.<br /> If you're a Mage that lays low, minds their own business and does not partake in the Ascension War or messes with sleepers, chances are high the Technocracy will actually leave you alone these days.<br /> It's kind of a &quot;You don't start messin', and we don't clean it up&quot; situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-05-2016, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:10:37-07:00","id":998898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/998847-what-stops-the-never-ending-arms-race?p=998855#post998855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pogrom is over. Has been for over a decade.<br /> If you're a Mage that lays low, minds their own business and does not partake in the Ascension War or messes with sleepers, chances are high the Technocracy will actually leave you alone these days.<br /> It's kind of a &quot;You don't start messin', and we don't clean it up&quot; situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they don't kill you just for existing. That doesn't stop the pressure to convert to science. And if you go around doing magic, eventually you're gonna go from harmless superstitionist to dangerous reality deviant on the list of problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T08:46:03-08:00","id":999234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/998847-what-stops-the-never-ending-arms-race#post998847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me, that thanks to the setting encouraging a somewhat militant mindset no matter WHAT faction you're aligned with, and the endless ways for mages to prepare for conflict, how do you guys prevent the game from turning into a mystical cold war for the soul of the world where the players are always working on that edge that will tip the odds in their favor just enough to turn the cold war hot?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In my games, i use the revised timeline (without the remaining avatar storm) and the botton line is &quot;nobody cares about the ascension war&quot; except inmature dickheads that cling to the past and wanna demonize the other side and they are treated as such. <br /> <br /> The technocracy has bigger fish to fry than getting rid of that hermetic dude that cast fireball from time to time agaisnt nephandi or weirder shit. Specially if said mage doesnt go around converting people to his paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T08:55:49-08:00","id":999243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/998847-what-stops-the-never-ending-arms-race?p=999234#post999234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In my games, i use the revised timeline (without the remaining avatar storm) and the botton line is &quot;nobody cares about the ascension war&quot; except inmature dickheads that cling to the past and wanna demonize the other side and they are treated as such.<br /> <br /> The technocracy has bigger fish to fry than getting rid of that hermetic dude that cast fireball from time to time agaisnt nephandi or weirder shit. Specially if said mage doesnt go around converting people to his paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what was in the above. The Ascension war has gone cold in the revised timeline, but it's hardly dead. The Technocracy has just switched to a nicer means of pursuing it than kicking down your door and shooting you in the face. Instead they try to win you over and convert you. They set up 'fair' guidelines so that when someone breaks them it's 'their fault' so the Traditions don't come down in full force.<br /> <br /> And, as the Void Engineers convention book shows, even in the revised era, it's considered tantamount to treason to work alongside Tradition mages barring highly exceptional circumstances, (Nephandi for example.) and even then it's distasteful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T12:03:30-08:00","id":999362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/998847-what-stops-the-never-ending-arms-race?p=999243#post999243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what was in the above. The Ascension war has gone cold in the revised timeline, but it's hardly dead. The Technocracy has just switched to a nicer means of pursuing it than kicking down your door and shooting you in the face. Instead they try to win you over and convert you. They set up 'fair' guidelines so that when someone breaks them it's 'their fault' so the Traditions don't come down in full force.<br /> <br /> And, as the Void Engineers convention book shows, even in the revised era, it's considered tantamount to treason to work alongside Tradition mages barring highly exceptional circumstances, (Nephandi for example.) and even then it's distasteful.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is ways to take the canonically &quot;cease fire&quot;, the question of the thread was &quot;how do you guys prevent the game from turning into a mystical cold war for the soul of the world where the players are always working on that edge that will tip the odds in their favor just enough to turn the cold war hot?&quot;<br /> <br /> My take is to make the war a non-issue or barely an issue. Focusing more on &quot;you got magic, now what? Question&quot; and leave the big world changing consensus as things of no bearing in the game, basically saying to the players &quot;look guys this is small scale game so you wont be punching the technocracy or leaving your paradigm aside to become demigods. Thats just not gonna happen on the confines of this campaign&quot;<br /> <br /> As much material saying that working with a traditionalist is treason and the cold war angle there as much material (Syndicate revised for example) saying that the technocracy is more focuses in cleaning house than fighting a scientifically proven useless war.<br /> <br /> In deep space-umbra my void engineers would use a hand by any mage against a threat when the other option is everyone dying considering they are the convention less invested in the Ascension war or the world consensus and the high command is less meticulous in deep space-umbra than otherwise be on the earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 11-06-2016, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T03:24:02-08:00","id":999649,"title":"","content":"In my game, I go with Revised's timeline as well, storm and all (though it's potency has waned a bit).<br /> <br /> The way I've done is by having the Technocracy acknowledge the heavy losses that the Ascension War has dealt them and is now shifting focus away from outright killing mages, and instead belittling and incentivising sleeper interest in the paradigm of Science. It's become a war of ideas rather than a war of guns.<br /> Because reality zones are a thing, the Technocracy are trying to expand the Scientific zones and erode at or outright remove any other zones with conflicting beliefs. This is they idea behind enforcing every child going to school and normalising college, that all countries receive western medicine, and that western style journalism becomes the global standard.<br /> <br /> The Tradition mages have restructured and got their New Council to work on, so politically speaking there's still a lot of work to be done in figuring out their own infrastructure before organised attacks can be even thought about let alone coordinated. As the Avatar storm still rages, albeit less so, Space exploration is still considered far too risky for either group, especially because of the constant threat of Nephandi, Marauders, and Threat Null. For the Traditions, this too means that creating Horizon realms is more trouble than it's worth, though that doesn't stop a number of hotheads from trying (and getting pretty far with it).<br /> <br /> That's how things are on a global level, but at a more local level it really is a case by case thing depending on the specific interests of the Technocrats and Mages within the local group. They might even start working together in order to combat a bigger threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T05:03:52-08:00","id":999670,"title":"","content":"You seem to propose a very potent Technocracy that can detect mystic mages when they cast even the least spell, and that has manpower to send a team to shoot each of them in the face. You can run that game if you want, but it limits your options as you've seen. Consider a Technocracy that's barely holding things together - not enough people, hypertech failing on you at the worst time, fires to put out on every continent and every plane of existence, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T07:42:39-08:00","id":999736,"title":"","content":"Have any of us considered Peacemakers? That is, powerful Mages - on both sides of the conflict - who encourage their sides to make nice, for the sake of peace. Maybe they desire peace for its own good, maybe they have a vested interest in preventing more fighting. Maybe they've just gotten used to the idea of a cease fire, and want to protect that status quo. Regardless, they work to smooth over conflicts and discourage aggressive actions. And to act as intermediaries between sides, to broker peace.<br /> <br /> This can happen with talking with more hawkish elements, pulling rank, or even cutting deals.<br /> <br /> &quot;Look kid, I understand your feelings. But this vendetta is only going to make innocents suffer, more of our guys buy it, and make the streets run red with blood. How about, if you drop this obsession, I give you access to copies of valuable arcane material? I know you've been looking to work your way towards Master training. I can make that happen...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}